WEBVTT

00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.310
Um, Mr. Kishibe.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.310
I have a big favor to ask today.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.270
KOICHI HIROSE, HIGH SCHOOL STUDENT

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:32.360
ROHAN KISHIBE, MANGA ARTIST

00:00:32.440 --> 00:00:34.360
Oh. What's that, Koichi?

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:39.990
Actually, I'm going to go abroad
this spring, during the school break.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.450
Are you? Where to?

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.830
To Italy.

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:44.750
Wha…!

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.080
Italy?

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:51.460
Could you please use your Heaven's Door
to write in for me, "I can speak Italian"?

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:56.090
Why on earth should I do
such a thing for you?

00:00:56.890 --> 00:01:01.810
I… I've never been abroad
on my own before, so I'm nervous.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:06.060
So, I'd like to be able
to at least speak the language!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:07.940
Please!

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.440
You're going to Italy, huh?

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.900
Then I'll tell you about
the experiences I had there.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:15.900
Huh?

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:19.910
When I first met you, I had to stop
drawing my series because of the injury

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:22.160
which <i>he</i> caused, remember?

00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:27.580
During that time, I went to Venice to do
some research for my next manga plot

00:01:27.670 --> 00:01:31.210
and stayed there on my own
for eight days or so.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.510
<i>That was when I came across this story.</i>

00:01:34.590 --> 00:01:36.090
<i>It's a really weird story.</i>

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:24.260
EPISODE 16: AT A CONFESSIONAL

00:02:30.480 --> 00:02:33.520
<i>The story I'm telling you is…</i>

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:37.240
<i>what I, Rohan Kishibe, heard</i>
<i>with my own ears.</i>

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:39.650
<i>It was a horrifying incident.</i>

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:45.540
<i>Do you know what a "confessional" is?</i>

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:50.420
<i>Every Italian church has one of those.</i>

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.540
<i>It has two wooden boxes</i>
<i>that look like telephone booths.</i>

00:02:54.340 --> 00:02:57.760
<i>The parish priest gets</i>
<i>in the one with the curtains</i>,

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:00.470
<i>and the parishioner goes in the other box.</i>

00:03:01.090 --> 00:03:03.930
<i>There's a little window</i>
<i>between the two boxes,</i>

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.930
<i>and voices can go</i>
<i>through the window, but…</i>

00:03:07.020 --> 00:03:10.060
<i>the priest and parishioner</i>
<i>cannot see each other.</i>

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:14.650
<i>The window allows the parishioner</i>
<i>to confess their "sins"</i>

00:03:15.150 --> 00:03:19.190
<i>with their privacy securely protected.</i>

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:25.580
<i>You see, you can't keep a secret</i>
<i>hidden deep in your heart for years.</i>

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:30.790
<i>The graver the secret is,</i>
<i>the greater the suffering of the heart.</i>

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:36.090
<i>A confessional is a place</i>
<i>to purge a soul of its sins.</i>

00:03:36.170 --> 00:03:38.210
<i>It was created</i>
<i>by the wisdom of people in the past.</i>

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:43.930
<i>It's not allowed, but I took some photos</i>
<i>when the priest wasn't around</i>

00:03:44.390 --> 00:03:47.970
<i>and looked closely at the design</i>
<i>and materials of the carvings.</i>

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:51.730
<i>And just for an experience,</i>

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:55.400
<i>I thought it wouldn't be a bad idea</i>
<i>if I could confess to a priest myself.</i>

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:56.980
<i>So I went in the box.</i>

00:03:57.650 --> 00:04:00.190
<i>The actual experience</i>
<i>would bring reality into my work, you see.</i>

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:14.370
Huh?

00:04:15.290 --> 00:04:18.800
Father, I've come to make a confession.

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:22.920
I have committed a great sin.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:23.930
<i>Wha…</i>

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:30.520
I can't stand it anymore.
I've got to tell you, Father.

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:35.600
I can't sleep
without making a confession.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:37.190
<i>I swear it!</i>

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:42.030
<i>At that time, I didn't know the box</i>
<i>with the curtains was for the priest.</i>

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:45.700
<i>This man mistook me for the priest.</i>

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:47.660
<i>But…</i>

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:50.200
<i>wasn't this a stroke of luck?</i>

00:04:52.290 --> 00:04:53.830
<i>What's his "great sin"?</i>

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:57.380
<i>I might as well</i>
<i>listen through to the end.</i>

00:04:57.460 --> 00:05:00.130
<i>A real experience</i>
<i>brings reality into my work.</i>

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:03.720
<i>It doesn't matter</i>
<i>who listens to his confession.</i>

00:05:03.800 --> 00:05:07.680
<i>After all, it's the thought</i>
<i>that he confessed to the priest</i>

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.100
<i>that matters for this man.</i>

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.970
Father, is there anything wrong?

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:20.570
No, it's nothing. Plea-- I mean, go on.

00:05:22.190 --> 00:05:24.820
Yes, but how do I start?

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:28.030
Well, that evening.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:33.410
<i>Yes, the whole thing</i>
<i>started on that evening.</i>

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:45.550
<i>I was 24 years old then,</i>

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:48.220
<i>and working at a food market.</i>

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:50.470
<i>I was doing manual labor.</i>

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:55.220
<i>I piled up sacks of corn on a truck</i>
<i>and carried them to the storehouse.</i>

00:05:55.810 --> 00:05:57.190
<i>It was hard work.</i>

00:05:57.640 --> 00:06:00.610
<i>I was so busy,</i>
<i>I didn't have time to meet any girls.</i>

00:06:01.110 --> 00:06:04.400
<i>I absolutely hated this job.</i>

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:09.860
<i>That evening, it was after 6:00 p.m.</i>

00:06:10.450 --> 00:06:12.660
<i>I was working overtime, as usual.</i>

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:17.370
<i>That's when that man appeared.</i>

00:06:20.330 --> 00:06:22.210
<i>He was staggering along</i>

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:26.170
<i>with empty eyes and unwashed hair.</i>
<i>He stank.</i>

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:28.220
<i>I could tell at once.</i>

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:30.390
<i>He was a tramp.</i>

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:34.680
Please… give me… something to eat.

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:36.850
<i>His voice was pathetic.</i>

00:06:37.730 --> 00:06:42.060
<i>He kept glancing</i>
<i>at my lunch on the table.</i>

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:44.820
<i>Suddenly, I started to feel angry.</i>

00:06:45.320 --> 00:06:47.440
<i>I've been working like a dog,</i>

00:06:47.530 --> 00:06:51.740
<i>while he's just been loafing around</i>
<i>behind the station or in a park.</i>

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:54.620
<i>He's got the nerve to ask for food!</i>

00:06:54.700 --> 00:06:55.870
<i>What a selfish jerk!</i>

00:06:56.910 --> 00:07:01.170
I work and get paid
and buy food with that money.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.250
Why don't you do the same?

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.380
I'll give you food <i>after</i> you carry
all these sacks to the storehouse.

00:07:08.460 --> 00:07:11.300
I… I will work.

00:07:11.840 --> 00:07:15.260
But first, please give me some food.

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:19.310
I haven't eaten for five days.
It's t-- true.

00:07:19.390 --> 00:07:24.520
Just a little bit of food.
I'll work after that, I promise!

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:26.070
Oh, really?

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:29.990
You only get paid
when you finish your job.

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:32.570
Are you gonna do it or not?

00:07:48.130 --> 00:07:51.840
Hey! Whatcha doing picking up
just that little one?

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:53.380
<i>These </i>ones are yours!

00:07:53.970 --> 00:07:56.260
Finish with these in an hour, okay?

00:07:56.350 --> 00:07:58.100
I wanna go home soon, you know!

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:03.690
Hurry up, for God's sake!

00:08:03.770 --> 00:08:06.810
If you wanna eat soon,
you've gotta finish soon!

00:08:07.900 --> 00:08:10.490
He's a lazy ass, that one.

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:16.200
He needs to learn a lesson.

00:08:30.340 --> 00:08:34.340
Hey! Don't pretend that you fell
just because you wanna slack off!

00:08:34.430 --> 00:08:36.970
You haven't even worked for ten minutes!

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:39.640
Slacking off?

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:44.020
Are you trying to tell me…

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:48.020
I look as if I'm slacking off?!

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:51.360
What the heck?!

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:56.360
I'm now deep in despair,
deeper than the dark sea…

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:58.570
because of you!

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:02.830
I'll never, ever forget your face!

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:07.170
I'll make you pay for this.

00:09:07.750 --> 00:09:09.790
I'll come back

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:14.050
at the happiest time of your life!
I will!

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:19.010
I will come back to get you.

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:20.850
So be prepared!

00:09:26.810 --> 00:09:30.230
Look!
There's someone lying under the sack!

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:34.030
He's dead!

00:09:35.030 --> 00:09:36.240
He is dead!

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:39.240
A doctor! Call a doctor!

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:41.160
Or call the police!

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:44.870
I didn't know!

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:50.080
I didn't know that
he really hadn't eaten for five days!

00:09:50.210 --> 00:09:53.050
Hang o-- I mean, wait a moment.

00:09:53.920 --> 00:09:58.260
Did you say the tramp spoke
for the last time… after he was dead?

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.970
Are you sure you were not dreaming?

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:02.970
Dreaming?

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:05.180
How I wish it were a dream.

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:10.480
The real terror
hadn't even started yet, Father.

00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:16.320
<i>After that, I suddenly got so lucky,</i>
<i>it felt almost eerie.</i>

00:10:17.240 --> 00:10:19.700
<i>I inherited some money</i>
<i>from a distant relative.</i>

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:22.070
<i>I won the jackpot in a soccer lottery.</i>

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:26.620
<i>I sold the land I bought with that money,</i>
<i>at a huge profit.</i>

00:10:27.160 --> 00:10:30.670
<i>Then I had the idea</i>
<i>to make snacks and food from corn</i>,

00:10:30.750 --> 00:10:33.170
<i>which became a huge hit</i>
<i>right after the launch.</i>

00:10:33.250 --> 00:10:35.550
<i>These products sold like hotcakes</i>
<i>all over the world.</i>

00:10:36.260 --> 00:10:40.010
<i>I'd had nothing to do with girls before,</i>
<i>but I got married</i>

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:44.470
<i>to a former supermodel who had appeared</i>
<i>at Milan Fashion Week.</i>

00:10:45.390 --> 00:10:48.480
<i>I had such a massive income,</i>
<i>I couldn't spend it all.</i>

00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:51.730
<i>Where I live now, I have 15 servants</i>

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:53.230
<i>and three chauffeurs.</i>

00:10:53.310 --> 00:10:56.190
<i>This outrageous good luck</i>
<i>always made me anxious.</i>

00:10:57.740 --> 00:11:02.570
<i>In the back of my mind,</i>
<i>I was always thinking of that dead man.</i>

00:11:08.790 --> 00:11:11.000
<i>Then I had a child.</i>

00:11:13.210 --> 00:11:14.710
Daddy! Daddy!

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:17.420
-<i>A cute girl, who looks like her mother.</i>
<i>-</i>Daddy!

00:11:18.130 --> 00:11:20.380
Daddy, look. Ready?

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:21.680
Keep looking!

00:11:26.930 --> 00:11:30.060
Oh, no! I missed!

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:33.020
Never mind! It was so close!

00:11:33.100 --> 00:11:37.110
You had your eyes closed, miss! Try again.

00:11:37.820 --> 00:11:38.650
Yeah!

00:11:39.570 --> 00:11:43.490
<i>As I watched my daughter playing</i>
<i>in the piazza…</i>

00:11:44.160 --> 00:11:50.410
<i>I couldn't help thinking,</i>
<i>"What a happy man I am."</i>

00:11:57.800 --> 00:11:59.460
As I promised…

00:12:04.140 --> 00:12:08.180
As I promised, I'm back.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.430
To get you, you miserable bastard!

00:12:12.440 --> 00:12:14.310
Are you all right, miss?

00:12:14.400 --> 00:12:15.270
Shut up!

00:12:18.650 --> 00:12:22.190
Don't worry. I'm just borrowing
your daughter's body.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:25.240
Stop! Stop it!

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:28.450
You're making a mistake!
It was all your own fault!

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:30.660
My own fault?

00:12:30.750 --> 00:12:35.670
The last few years,
you've had all the luck you need, eh?

00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:38.420
Wealth… fame… family… eh?

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:42.170
Did you think you got them
all by yourself?

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:45.430
See, I've been helping you secretly!

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:49.100
So when you fall from your pedestal,

00:12:49.180 --> 00:12:54.140
you'll taste what I felt-- despair!

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:56.690
However…

00:12:56.770 --> 00:13:01.730
I'm getting my revenge
so my soul can be saved.

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:08.160
But if you die thinking I killed you,
although it was my fault, I'll feel bad.

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:10.660
So I'll give you a chance.

00:13:10.740 --> 00:13:13.750
If it's my fault or not

00:13:13.830 --> 00:13:16.210
will be judged by God.

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:21.420
We'll see if you've got any future.
You try your luck.

00:13:21.500 --> 00:13:27.340
If destiny is on your side,
then my grudge would be baseless.

00:13:27.430 --> 00:13:29.970
So I won't kill you. I'll just disappear.

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:33.390
Destiny will be our judge, you see.

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:37.100
Do you wanna try your luck or not?

00:13:37.190 --> 00:13:40.110
I don't know what you are talking about.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:44.690
All you need to say is yes or no!

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:47.530
Why… why me?!

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:48.860
Answer me!

00:13:48.950 --> 00:13:52.120
If you don't wanna try,
I'll just cut your head off!

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:57.540
I'll try… I will try!

00:13:58.120 --> 00:14:01.040
I don't have a choice, do I?

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:02.880
Good.

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:04.510
Take it!

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:11.180
You can see your destiny
through a trivial, little thing.

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:15.350
Throw the popcorn
higher than that street lamp

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.140
and catch it with your mouth.

00:14:17.230 --> 00:14:18.940
Three times in a row.

00:14:19.020 --> 00:14:23.480
If you succeed, destiny is on your side
so I'll give up and disappear.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:25.650
Can such a trivial thing…?!

00:14:26.240 --> 00:14:29.450
This is also about my soul!

00:14:29.530 --> 00:14:31.820
Do you call it trivial?

00:14:33.160 --> 00:14:35.330
Start when I clap my hands.

00:14:35.410 --> 00:14:39.670
If the popcorn doesn't go high enough
or you start late, I'll kill you.

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:42.290
Ready? Go!

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:44.000
W-wait a moment!

00:14:49.050 --> 00:14:52.220
The height is okay.

00:14:52.890 --> 00:14:55.680
Why is this happening to me?

00:14:55.760 --> 00:14:58.600
There! It's coming down in front of me!

00:14:59.850 --> 00:15:01.980
No! Oh, no!

00:15:04.020 --> 00:15:05.020
I can't see!

00:15:13.320 --> 00:15:15.200
That was close!

00:15:15.280 --> 00:15:17.450
But I did it! I did it!

00:15:17.540 --> 00:15:19.160
I caught it!

00:15:21.460 --> 00:15:23.330
Now the second throw!

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:25.420
Get the next one ready.

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:26.960
W-wait a minute.

00:15:27.050 --> 00:15:29.760
Just now, the sun blinded me.

00:15:30.380 --> 00:15:32.130
But I can do it in the shade, right?

00:15:32.760 --> 00:15:35.550
Whatcha gonna demand next?

00:15:36.680 --> 00:15:40.060
Now is the time!
And here is the place!

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:42.810
Two more times! Okay?

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:45.520
If you fail, I'll kill ya!

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:49.400
If you succeed,
I'll disappear like I said.

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:52.910
Now do it! Your second throw!

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:58.830
You're… really gonna disappear, right?

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:03.580
If I succeed, you'll spare me, okay!

00:16:03.670 --> 00:16:05.080
Enough!

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:07.920
If you don't throw now, I'll kill you!

00:16:12.550 --> 00:16:15.220
Yes! The sun's gone behind a cloud.

00:16:15.890 --> 00:16:18.010
It's coming straight down!

00:16:20.270 --> 00:16:21.230
What?!

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:27.360
What the…!

00:16:29.020 --> 00:16:33.450
This is great!
They think you are feeding them.

00:16:46.880 --> 00:16:49.630
I did it! Serves you right!

00:16:49.710 --> 00:16:51.550
I've caught the second one too!

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.760
Look at that! It's dead easy.

00:16:54.840 --> 00:16:58.220
I was panicking, but now I'm calming down.

00:16:58.800 --> 00:17:01.180
I can do it! I can win!

00:17:01.270 --> 00:17:06.650
You can celebrate as much as you like,
after the last one.

00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:08.730
Are you ready?

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:10.270
Yeah! Bring it!

00:17:10.360 --> 00:17:13.440
I'll do it one more t--

00:17:24.290 --> 00:17:27.580
What the hell?!

00:17:28.330 --> 00:17:32.210
It's you who brought down these pigeons.

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:36.180
Who was it who scattered
the whole packet of popcorn?

00:17:36.260 --> 00:17:38.300
It was you!

00:17:41.100 --> 00:17:43.350
This… this last one.

00:17:44.060 --> 00:17:46.440
If I throw it higher than the lamp….

00:17:48.400 --> 00:17:50.520
Go away, just buzz off!

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:52.980
No more food for you!

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:56.030
Go! The last time!

00:17:56.110 --> 00:17:57.490
Wait! Wait a minute!

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:13.210
Ha! Pigeons can't eat burning popcorn!

00:18:13.300 --> 00:18:17.130
I put oil on it and lit it.
They won't eat that.

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:21.350
Yes! It's coming straight down!

00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:30.560
I can't see the burning popcorn.

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:33.520
I can't see it against the sun.

00:18:34.360 --> 00:18:35.230
I can't see it!

00:18:36.030 --> 00:18:37.690
I can't see it!

00:18:37.780 --> 00:18:39.740
Wh-- where is it?!

00:18:50.670 --> 00:18:56.340
The judgment says… it was not my fault!

00:19:16.020 --> 00:19:21.820
You're thinking,
"But he's alive," aren't you, Father?

00:19:22.820 --> 00:19:26.410
That's exactly why I came here.

00:19:27.410 --> 00:19:32.330
I can't stand not telling anyone
the terrible sin I've committed.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:39.630
That tramp had made me so rich
that I could get anything I wanted.

00:19:40.670 --> 00:19:45.300
So rich that I could easily find a servant
who would do anything I told him.

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:47.890
Master…

00:19:48.640 --> 00:19:50.060
come out.

00:19:52.020 --> 00:19:53.770
Master…

00:19:54.520 --> 00:20:00.740
No matter how many times you confess,
my curse will never leave you.

00:20:12.920 --> 00:20:17.630
You paid me to have cosmetic surgery.

00:20:18.250 --> 00:20:23.050
You cheated me
and threw me into such terror.

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:28.510
I'll never forgive you.
I'll never forget my grudge!

00:20:32.810 --> 00:20:35.560
You can follow me even into the church?

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:37.980
I curse you!

00:20:38.570 --> 00:20:44.950
When your daughter's having the happiest
time of her life, I'll come and get you.

00:20:46.450 --> 00:20:48.160
No good coming to get him.

00:20:48.740 --> 00:20:52.660
From now on, we'll watch you all the time

00:20:52.750 --> 00:20:56.170
so you can never cheat us!

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:15.980
Ooh, that's so scary!

00:21:16.060 --> 00:21:17.480
Okuyasu!

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:18.860
Yukako!

00:21:18.940 --> 00:21:22.610
Rohan, is that story true?

00:21:22.690 --> 00:21:26.610
Hey, lady, can I have a bubble milk tea?

00:21:27.160 --> 00:21:29.240
Where've you sprung from?

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:31.700
Are you saying I'm lying?

00:21:32.200 --> 00:21:34.620
Nah, I don't mean that…

00:21:35.210 --> 00:21:38.580
Could be it's just some run-in
between Stand Users

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:41.920
and nothing to do with vengeful ghosts?

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:44.460
Anyway, that sounds like
a really patient ghost.

00:21:44.550 --> 00:21:49.260
To be haunted for life! I'd go crazy…

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:53.720
Koichi, if a ghost starts haunting you,
you just tell me right away.

00:21:53.810 --> 00:21:56.560
I'll get rid of it once and for all!

00:21:57.140 --> 00:22:00.060
Oh, yeah, thanks.

00:22:07.110 --> 00:22:12.030
<i>What's become of him since?</i>
<i>I, Rohan Kishibe, don't yet know.</i>

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:14.620
<i>Next year or the year after…</i>

00:22:15.120 --> 00:22:19.040
<i>I might as well go there again to see him.</i>

00:22:20.250 --> 00:22:23.000
<i>He wouldn't give up</i>
<i>when the ghost haunted him.</i>

00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:26.010
<i>He faces life alone, but optimistically.</i>

00:22:26.800 --> 00:22:28.680
<i>I think he's evil,</i>

00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:31.350
<i>but I can admire his resilience.</i>

00:22:33.640 --> 00:22:37.480
<i>Maybe I'm the only one to think so.</i>

00:24:15.160 --> 00:24:17.490
Subtitle translation by Songju Chong
